cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "K-CheckupDx-Bench: a benchmark for tiered determination in the Korean National Health Screening Program"
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
version: "1.1"
date-released: "2026-09-01"
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nccaiteam/K-CheckupDx-Bench"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22218041"
abstract: >-
  Evaluation data and tooling for tiered determination (Normal A / Normal B / suspected disease)
  in the Korean National Health Screening Program, derived entirely from published criteria.
  Includes a 144-case tier set, a 528-case / 6,321-pair value-ladder set for the label-independent
  monotonicity violation metric, a 54-case BMI source-ambiguity set, the intermediate ladder
  versions v1.1 and v1.2 retained for the confound audit trail, a deterministic rule engine
  that re-derives every gold label, and the complete result files for all reported runs.
keywords:
  - health screening
  - large language models
  - benchmark
  - clinical numeracy
  - monotonicity
  - Korean
